# Overrides for scripts/run_test.py — copy to .env.test and fill in.
#
# This file is layered ON TOP of .env, so it only needs the settings that DIFFER. Everything else
# (GEMINI_API_KEY, the service-account key, timezone) is inherited, which is what makes the test a
# real test: same model, same code path — different mailbox, different destination.
#
# run_test.py refuses to start if the mailbox or the sheet is still the client's.

# ---- Your test mailbox -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# A Gmail of your own is easiest: turn on 2-Step Verification, then create an app password.
# To give it something to transcribe, email a .wav to it — the pipeline only cares that a message
# has an audio attachment. Forwarding one of the client's voicemail emails gives you realistic
# audio; just remember those rows then hold a real caller's details.
IMAP_PROVIDER=gmail
IMAP_USERNAME=
IMAP_PASSWORD=
IMAP_MAILBOX=INBOX
# 14 days, not 2: a test mailbox is usually seeded by forwarding voicemails that are already a
# week or two old, and a short window silently excludes every one of them. Each pass re-transcribes
# everything in the window, so this is also what you turn DOWN if the Gemini calls add up.
IMAP_SINCE_DAYS=14

# IMPORTANT — clear the client's filters. .env narrows the search to their voicemail sender and
# subject; inherited into your mailbox those match nothing, and every run finds 0 voicemails while
# looking perfectly healthy. Leaving these empty means "any message carrying audio".
VOICEMAIL_FROM=
VOICEMAIL_SUBJECT=

# The "Open email" column. The Gmail form works if your test mailbox is Gmail; it is NOT
# transferable between providers ({gm_msgid} is a Gmail-only IMAP extension), so it has to match
# whatever mailbox you set above. Leave empty for no link column.
EMAIL_LINK_TEMPLATE=https://mail.google.com/mail/u/0/#all/{gm_msgid}

# ---- Your test sheet -------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create a sheet of your own and share it with the service account's client_email as an Editor,
# exactly like the client's. The id is the long string from the URL:
#   docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS_PART>/edit
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=

# The tab must already exist, spelled exactly. Quote it if the name has a space:
#   SHEET_RANGE='Voicemail tests'!A1
SHEET_RANGE=Voicemails!A1

# ---- Handled for you; no need to set these ---------------------------------------------------
#   STATE_FILE   forced to .processed.test.json, so a test pass can never mark the client's
#                voicemails as done and make their poller skip them forever.
#   BACKEND_URL  suppressed unless you run with --report, so test passes stay out of the client's
#                dashboard numbers.
#
# Sometimes worth overriding while testing:
# EXTRACT_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite
# BUSINESS_TIMEZONE=America/Los_Angeles

# ---- The voice agent's taken messages -------------------------------------------------------
# scripts/write_agent_messages.py pulls the messages the assistant took (a caller who wanted an
# appointment and could not be put through) and writes them into the sheet above, in the same
# columns as a voicemail. Both must be set, and both are ignored by the voicemail pipeline.
#
# All four must be set HERE. The writer will not fall back to .env for any of them, because a key
# that inherits silently is exactly how a test run reaches the client's data.
#
#   GOOGLE_SHEET_ID   the test sheet (already set above). This is the ONE value that must DIFFER
#                     from .env — it alone decides which document is written to.
#   SHEET_RANGE       the tab in it (already set above). May be the same name as the client's: it
#                     is a heading inside a different document.
#   BACKEND_URL       where the agent records its calls. Normally the same as .env — there is one
#                     backend.
#   AGENT_CONFIG_KEY  the same shared key the agent uses. Normally the same as .env.
BACKEND_URL=
AGENT_CONFIG_KEY=
